<title>FRANCE: Lagardere rises on Thomson hopes.</title>
<headline>Lagardere rises on Thomson hopes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French conglomerate Groupe Lagardere traded higher on Thursday on a newspaper report that the parliamentary defence committee favours its bid in the Thomson SA privatisation, traders said.</p>
<p>Business daily Les Echos reported that the committee, which visited the Farnborough air show in Britain, considers Lagardere a better candidate than Alcatel Alsthom to take over the electronics group, on the lines of &quot;industrial logic.&quot;</p>
<p>Lagardere was up 3.80 francs at 121.50, or 3.14 percent, at 1304 GMT, while the market was up 0.31 percent. Lagardere wants to merge its Matra defence unit with Thomson-CSF.</p>
</text>
